&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 120%; mso-outline-level: 1;"&gt;&lt;a name="Section2"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 11.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;WISCONSIN RIVER POWER COMPANY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 120%;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 11.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 120%;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 11.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;NOTES TO REGULATORY BASIS FINANCIAL STATEMENTS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 120%; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 11.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;AS OF AND FOR THE YEARS ENDED JUNE 30, 2026 AND 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 120%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="WordSection3"&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 120%; mso-outline-level: 2;"&gt;&lt;a name="Section3"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 11pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;"&gt;NOTE A--FERC FORM 1 REPORTING COMPARED TO GENERALLY ACCEPTED ACCOUNTING PRINCIPLES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 120%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 11.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 120%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;The accompanying financial statements have been prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC as set forth in the Uniform System of Accounts and accounting releases, which differ from GAAP. The principal differences for Wisconsin River Power Company ("us," "we," or "our") have no impact on the reported net income. As required by the FERC, we reclassify certain items in our Form 1 in a manner different from the presentation in the GAAP Financial Statements, as described below:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 120%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 13.5pt; text-indent: -13.5pt; line-height: 120%; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 13.0pt;"&gt;&lt;!-- [if !supportLists]--&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8226;&lt;span style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;!--[endif]--&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Removal costs that do not have an associated legal obligation are recognized as a component of accumulated depreciation, whereas these costs are recognized for GAAP as a regulatory liability.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 120%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 13.5pt; text-indent: -13.5pt; line-height: 120%; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 13.0pt;"&gt;&lt;!-- [if !supportLists]--&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8226;&lt;span style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;!--[endif]--&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;The GAAP financial statements are reported in accordance with the Income Taxes Topic of the FASB Accounting Standards Codification, whereas the Form 1 is reported in accordance with the FERC-issued accounting guidance. As such, in the Form 1, interest and penalties on tax deficiencies are not reported as income tax expense. Additionally, GAAP allows netting of deferred tax assets and liabilities whereas FERC requires a gross presentation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 120%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 13.5pt; text-indent: -13.5pt; line-height: 120%; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 13.0pt;"&gt;&lt;!-- [if !supportLists]--&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8226;&lt;span style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;!--[endif]--&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;As required by FERC, we classify certain items in our Form 1 Comparative Balance Sheet (primarily the components of certain miscellaneous current and accrued liabilities, deferred debits, and deferred credits) in a manner different than required by GAAP.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 120%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 13.5pt; text-indent: -13.5pt; line-height: 120%; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 13.0pt;"&gt;&lt;!-- [if !supportLists]--&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8226;&lt;span style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;!--[endif]--&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Operating revenues reported in Account 400 consist of amounts billable to our two wholesale customers under long term contracts. See Note 2, Related Parties, and Note 3, Operating Revenues, for more information.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 13.5pt; text-indent: -13.5pt; line-height: 120%; tab-stops: 13.0pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 13.5pt; text-indent: -13.5pt; line-height: 120%; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 13.0pt;"&gt;&lt;!-- [if !supportLists]--&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8226;&lt;span style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;!--[endif]--&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;The non-service cost components of our net periodic benefit costs are recorded as a component of operating expenses, whereas GAAP requires these costs to be recorded outside of operating income. In addition, the non-service components of our net periodic benefit costs that are capitalized to utility plant are reported as a regulatory asset or liability under GAAP.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 120%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="WordSection4" style="font-size: 14px;"&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 16.8px;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
