&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 13.5pt; text-indent: -13.5pt; line-height: 120%; mso-pagination: lines-together; page-break-after: avoid; tab-stops: 13.0pt;"&gt;&lt;sup&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;(1)&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;State taxes in Wisconsin made up the majority of the tax effect in this category.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 115%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 13.5pt; text-indent: -13.5pt; line-height: 120%; tab-stops: 13.0pt;"&gt;&lt;sup&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;(2)&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;AFUDC-Equity represents the cost of capital (i.e. ROE) that is added to the construction cost of an asset while it is being built. The tax benefit for regulated utilities from AFUDC-Equity is a regulatory gross-up to allow the recovery of income taxes on the equity portion of construction costs, even though it is not a tax deductible expense.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 120%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
